   "cooked": "<p>I forked <a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/TEC-Hatch-Vote/issues/33\">Sem’s proposal</a> to make:</p><aside class=\"onebox githubissue\">\n<header class=\"source\">\n<a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/TEC-Hatch-Vote/issues/35\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">github.com/CommonsBuild/TEC-Hatch-Vote</a>\n</header>\n<article class=\"onebox-body\">\n<div class=\"github-row\">\n<div class=\"github-icon-container\" title=\"Issue\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"github-icon\" height=\"60\" viewbox=\"0 0 14 16\" width=\"60\"><path d=\"M7 2.3c3.14 0 5.7 2.56 5.7 5.7s-2.56 5.7-5.7 5.7A5.71 5.71 0 0 1 1.3 8c0-3.14 2.56-5.7 5.7-5.7zM7 1C3.14 1 0 4.14 0 8s3.14 7 7 7 7-3.14 7-7-3.14-7-7-7zm1 3H6v5h2V4zm0 6H6v2h2v-2z\"></path></svg>\n</div>\n<div class=\"github-info-container\">\n<h4>\n<a href=\"https://github.com/CommonsBuild/TEC-Hatch-Vote/issues/35\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Forking the baby (Jiving on #33)</a>\n</h4>\n<div class=\"github-info\">\n<div class=\"date\">\n        opened <span class=\"discourse-local-date\" data-date=\"2021-05-05\" data-format=\"ll\" data-time=\"13:48:09\" data-timezone=\"UTC\">01:48PM - 05 May 21 UTC</span>\n</div>\n<div class=\"user\">\n<a href=\"https://github.com/GriffGreen\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">\n<img alt=\"GriffGreen\" class=\"onebox-avatar-inline\" height=\"20\" src=\"https://forum.tecommons.org/uploads/default/original/1X/9e4a7471173735a334e3d7a3e748307a3f2ca638.png\" width=\"20\"/>\n          GriffGreen\n        </a>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"github-row\">\n<p class=\"github-content\">Check out my proposal for the Hatch! Click here to preload the Hatch Configuration Dashboard with my parameters if you think...</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"labels\">\n<span style=\"display:inline-block;margin-top:2px;background-color: #B8B8B8;padding: 2px;border-radius: 4px;color: #fff;margin-left: 3px;\">Vote</span>\n</div>\n</article>\n<div class=\"onebox-metadata\">\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear: both\"></div>\n</aside>\n<p>I want to shill the idea of a very high support required (90% min) so that we as a community have a high consensus threshold for the next step… imagine if 25% of the people vote no to the commons upgrade… that is a bad sign! We shouldn’t let it pass.</p>\n<p><em>end rant</em></p>",
